    thinking: "**Generating Stunning Images**\n\nI\'ve successfully generated four high-quality images. Specifically, I created: /src/assets/images/profile_1781816280057.jpg, /src/assets/images/velostat_top_1781816294339.jpg, and /src/assets/images/fsr_1_17818163... (the last file name is truncated). The initial results are quite promising.\n\n\n**Mapping Image Paths**\n\nI\'m now focusing on efficiently integrating the generated images into the React application. The initial thought was to directly map the images, but I\'m leaning toward placing them in the `/public/images/` folder for simpler access through both relative imports and public paths. I considered using a script, but the available `shell_exec` command limitations prevent arbitrary shell command execution. I am now exploring alternative methods to achieve this.\n\n\n**Refining Integration Approach**\n\nI\'ve realized that using Vite allows direct importing from the `/src/assets/images/` directory, which is ideal. It streamlines the React component integration, and simplifies the bundling. Further, I\'ve confirmed image paths: `/src/assets/images/profile_1781816280057.jpg`, `/src/assets/images/velostat_top_1781816294339.jpg`, `/src/assets/images/fsr_1_1781816311419.jpg`, and `/src/assets/images/blindspot_1_1781816326394.jpg`. However, the deployment requirement creates a tension that is now under review.\n\n\n**Designing Static Export**\n\nI am now focused on a Static Export Panel within the React app, directly addressing the portfolio\'s theme. The design emphasizes instant accessibility to static HTML, CSS, and JS code. I\'m exploring an interactive UI section for single-file copies, aligning with the goal of \"Engineering precision and transparency\". I want users to readily obtain standalone versions of core files for deployment, and to have a physical representation of the static files on disk. The physical files I\'m generating would include index.html, style.css, script.js, and resume.pdf, alongside an images directory.\n\n\n**Refining Export Strategy**\n\nI\'ve hit on a brilliant plan! The active live preview will stay as the React app, or can be compiled to a static site. On disk, I\'m creating static files like `/style.css`, `/script.js`, and updating `/index.html` or creating separate static files in `/static/`. A ZIP export would include a complete vanilla project. I\'m focusing on making `/src/App.tsx` a modular React app suitable for the AI Studio. I also aim for a custom \"Resume\" download using a PDF generator or SVG print-preview.\n\n\n**Defining Portfolio Style**\n\nI am now meticulously crafting the portfolio\'s visual style. The integration of a copy-to-clipboard code viewer is crucial for demonstrating clean coding practices. I\'m choosing \"Inter\" for UI, \"Space Grotesk\" for display, and \"JetBrains Mono\" for code snippets. The color palette will feature a dark charcoal background, a rich red primary accent, and carefully selected complementary colors to evoke a Porsche/Apple design aesthetic. A modular architecture is also being developed, and I\'ve started defining core types for projects and experiences.\n\n\n\n**Structuring Component Design**\n\nI\'m now deep in defining the structural architecture for a stellar portfolio. I\'m focusing on key components: a sticky, transitioning `Navbar`, a dynamic `Hero` section with an interactive background, a bold `About` section highlighting core metrics, a `Projects` section featuring image slides and an interactive CAD inspect mode, and an experience timeline in `Experience`. Aesthetic `Skills` categorization, an interactive `ExportPanel` (simulating a terminal), a modern `Contact` grid, and a refined `Footer` complete the component suite.\n\n\n"
